WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.384
Agent latency includes every model request, tool call, queue wait, and retry.

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.701
A three-step agent can be much slower than one completion.

00:00:08.851 --> 00:00:13.180
Propagate a total deadline and reserve enough time for final response assembly.

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:19.085
Use finite retries with jitter for retryable failures, and avoid automatically retrying

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:20.045
non-idempotent actions.

00:00:20.195 --> 00:00:25.338
Concurrency limits protect model providers, database pools, and tool services.

00:00:25.488 --> 00:00:29.595
A circuit breaker can temporarily stop calls to a failing dependency.

00:00:29.745 --> 00:00:32.330
Rate limits and token budgets protect spend.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:36.817
Cache only results whose scope, freshness, and privacy rules are understood; a

00:00:36.817 --> 00:00:40.793
cache key that omits tenant identity can become a data leak.

00:00:40.942 --> 00:00:44.153
OllamaModel has a connection timeout and request timeout.

00:00:44.303 --> 00:00:47.122
Agent checks its total deadline between steps.

00:00:47.272 --> 00:00:51.233
If the provider returns 503, the lab fails clearly instead of treating

00:00:51.233 --> 00:00:53.213
the body as a model answer.

00:00:53.363 --> 00:00:58.046
The teaching adapter does not implement automatic retries, which keeps the failure

00:00:58.046 --> 00:01:00.388
path explicit for the first exercises.

00:01:00.538 --> 00:01:04.117
Simulate a slow model endpoint and a 503 response.

00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:08.404
Add at most one retry for a read-only model request, with a

00:01:08.404 --> 00:01:09.094
remaining-budget check.

00:01:09.244 --> 00:01:12.859
Measure how retry traffic behaves under ten concurrent users.

00:01:13.009 --> 00:01:16.204
Stop when the remaining budget cannot support another attempt.

00:01:16.354 --> 00:01:20.032
Avoid retrying validation errors or unauthorized requests.

00:01:20.182 --> 00:01:23.282
Compare success rate against added traffic and latency.

00:01:23.432 --> 00:01:28.259
A successful retry policy should improve useful outcomes without amplifying an outage

00:01:28.259 --> 00:01:29.466
into uncontrolled load.

00:01:29.616 --> 00:01:30.287
Question.

00:01:30.437 --> 00:01:32.936
What is the unit of AI cost optimization?

00:01:33.086 --> 00:01:33.663
Answer.

00:01:33.813 --> 00:01:38.664
Cost per successfully completed task under the required quality and safety constraints,

00:01:38.664 --> 00:01:40.686
not merely cost per token.

00:01:40.836 --> 00:01:41.507
Question.

00:01:41.657 --> 00:01:43.866
Why can retries make outages worse?

00:01:44.016 --> 00:01:44.592
Answer.

00:01:44.742 --> 00:01:48.688
They multiply traffic when the dependency has the least spare capacity.
